[{"id":2729687560,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6is7oI","state":"CHANGES_REQUESTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?u=68d23e7ee9cdf810da125e8510b72f845b9dccc8&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","login":"Calinou","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou"},"body":"The property should only be shown if **Size Limit** is greater than 0, as it's not effective otherwise. Also, it should be moved below **Size Limit**.\r\n\r\nTo conditionally hide the option according to **Size Limit**, modify this method:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/ba3482926daa6450d21b030cfe029689525c0e51/editor/import/resource_importer_texture.cpp#L183-L213\r\n\r\nThen add this property usage in the `size_limit` property binding: `PROPERTY_USAGE_DEFAULT | PROPERTY_USAGE_UPDATE_ALL_IF_MODIFIED`\r\n\r\nAlso, it may be worth considering renaming the property to something different like **Size Limit Interpolation**, so its linking to **Size Limit** is more explicit.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104813#pullrequestreview-2729687560","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104813","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-03-31T15:25:55Z"},{"id":2787937091,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6mLItD","state":"COMMENTED","commit_id":"26ba9556d020eee185f5897cb5d541dddb3ae6f3","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?u=6e9313e254649f6dc55e92536596487ac10bf5a2&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","login":"